<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_ScaldExposure.xml                  TerminalBiomes
  ==========================================================================
  SCALD_STEAM_WEATHER_DESIGN_1 step 4 ("Exposure clock"), built
  2026-09-26. RUT_ScaldSteamCarrier (../GameConditionDefs/) grants this
  hediff to every eligible pawn so its own comp can run at all.

  The clock's protection stat is vanilla ArmorRating_Heat, summed over worn
  apparel (SCALD_FOLD_INTO_HEAT_1, decision taken by question card
  2026-10-08: one kind of heat, and a steam burn is an injury, so heat
  ARMOR answers it, not insulation). Any heat-armored garment slows it.

  The owner's brief was one sentence: make the steam "beautiful and
  interesting (and deadly without protective gear)". This def is the deadly
  half, and the ruling that sizes it is his, by question card 2026-09-25:
  **unprotected in the steam, dead in under two days.**

  ⚠️ EVERY NUMBER BELOW IS INVENTED except the shape of that ruling. The
  spec states them and this file ships them unchanged:
    severityPerDayExposed  0.6   -> ~1.7 days unprotected to the top stage
    severityPerDayUnexposed -0.35 -> heals off in ~3 days roofed or on a
                                     still day
    minDriveFactor         0.08  -> Ban 3. Gear NEVER zeroes the clock; at
                                     full protection it still runs at 8%.
  Stage thresholds 0.15 / 0.35 / 0.6 / 0.85 and their capMods are likewise
  the spec's own INVENTED ladder. Only the top stage is lethal.

  onlyDuringWeather RUT_ScaldSteam is the whole rhythm of the mechanic: on
  a still day (RUT_ScaldSteamLock's Clear burst, MTB 96h for 12-24h) the
  clock STOPS and starts unwinding. That is what makes the still day
  strategically loud — it is the window to salvage the wrecks, cross the
  shallows and work the vents without paying.

  The comp additionally stops the clock under a roof (its own onlyUnroofed
  gate) — so a roof is the free, always-available answer, and the spec's
  protection table lists it first on purpose.

  🔴 immuneThingDefs are the Scald's own natives. This is the STEAM half of
  native immunity; the WATER half is a different mechanism entirely
  (RM_OrganicScaldNative, the HediffGiverSetDef that drops
  HediffGiver_Terrain, on each race). Both are needed; neither substitutes
  for the other. Any future Scald native must be added to BOTH — the race
  file's own header carries the water half's version of this rule.
  ⚠️ The list below names only the two races that existed before
  2026-09-26; the seven added by SEA_FISHABLES_ALIVE_IN_DEPTHS_1
  (RM_ScaldFloorFauna.xml) are here too, because a creature made of the
  boil should not be scalded by its own sky.

  MayRequire is load-bearing: the comp class and its properties type both
  live in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards, and an unresolvable comp class
  discards the whole def silently (see the same note on
  RUT_MiasmaExposure.xml).
-->
<Defs>

  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RUT_ScaldExposure</defName>
    <label>scald exposure</label>
    <description>Live steam, breathed and worn. The Scald's sky is the lake's own breath and it is clean — which does not make it safe: it is water at the boil, standing over everything, and skin and lungs take it the way they take any steam. Under a roof, or on one of the rare still days, it starts to come off.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.85,0.95,0.95)</defaultLabelColor>
    <minSeverity>0.0001</minSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>0.0001</initialSeverity>
    <makesSickThought>true</makesSickThought>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <lethalSeverity>1.0</lethalSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>onset</label>
        <becomeVisible>false</becomeVisible>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.15</minSeverity>
        <label>damp</label>
        <!-- No effect at all: the warning line, so the player learns the
             mechanic before it costs anything. -->
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.35</minSeverity>
        <label>scalded skin</label>
        <painOffset>0.15</painOffset>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <offset>-0.10</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.6</minSeverity>
        <label>steam-burned</label>
        <painOffset>0.35</painOffset>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Breathing</capacity>
            <offset>-0.30</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.20</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>-0.10</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <minSeverity>0.85</minSeverity>
        <label>boiled</label>
        <painOffset>0.5</painOffset>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Breathing</capacity>
            <offset>-0.60</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>-0.40</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
    </stages>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.HediffCompProperties_EnvironmentalExposure">
        <onlyDuringWeather>RUT_ScaldSteam</onlyDuringWeather>
        <severityPerDayExposed>0.6</severityPerDayExposed>
        <severityPerDayUnexposed>-0.35</severityPerDayUnexposed>
        <protectionStat>ArmorRating_Heat</protectionStat>
        <minDriveFactor>0.08</minDriveFactor>
        <affects>Flesh</affects>
        <immuneThingDefs>
          <li>RM_Noohm</li>
          <li>RM_Shulla</li>
          <li>RM_Eesh</li>
          <li>RM_Doss</li>
          <li>RM_Muddal</li>
          <li>RM_Thuum</li>
          <li>RM_Karrash</li>
          <li>RM_Ekkel</li>
          <li>RM_Bladderboil</li>
        </immuneThingDefs>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
